      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalist interpretations of the Second Amendment, which emphasize the framers' intent, argue that the right to bear arms is strictly tied to militia service and is not an individual right. Living constitutionalists, on the other hand, believe the Second Amendment should be interpreted in the context of modern society, viewing it as an individual right that adapts to contemporary needs. This tension reflects broader ideological divides, with originalists often aligning with conservative views that prioritize historical context and living constitutionalists with liberal perspectives that emphasize evolving societal norms.",
